From f8b00b7ac7ac03730361ce45a534887db917d305 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:36:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] inrun (scratch): pace leaves body=default -- it climbs
 fast under selection and costs frame time

8-seed hA1 pilot, 6 rounds x 200k: pace +0.2 -> +0.5 (bodyD) and +0.72
(hgbodyD) by r3-r5. hgbodyD_1's r5 founders, one 60k round with selection
off: 8,961 frames/s with their evolved pace against 13,443 with pace held
at the founding body, on fewer live ants (9.2 against 11.9).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DWLmVnMuZT7iPWY73DvPhf
---
 examples/inrun.rs | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/examples/inrun.rs b/examples/inrun.rs
index 09a90b15..47b546fd 100644
--- a/examples/inrun.rs
+++ b/examples/inrun.rs
@@ -64,8 +64,10 @@ type Body = [f32; organism::CREATURE_TRAITS];
 /// nor billed); the walk, trail-plane, door and forage-memory genes (read only by the game ant's own walk and `act`,
 /// which a mind replaces); armour (billed every tick and never bitten here, so it could only fall); dig_force (one
 /// step down from 1.0 below packed soil's 0.95 leaves an ant that cannot cut spoil -- a cheap jaw selection would take
-/// while digging is already being bred out).
-const BODY_DEFAULT: [&str; 5] = ["appetite", "digest_rate", "crop_capacity", "gut_bias", "pace"];
+/// while digging is already being bred out); pace (selection takes it up fast -- +0.2 to +0.5..0.7 in 6 rounds of an
+/// 8-seed pilot on hA1 -- and a quick ant takes more turns per frame: an evolved colony ran at 8,961 frames/s against
+/// 13,443 with pace held at the founding body, on fewer live ants (9.2 against 11.9). `pace` still opens by name).
+const BODY_DEFAULT: [&str; 4] = ["appetite", "digest_rate", "crop_capacity", "gut_bias"];
 
 /// A child's body under `body=`: the parent's open genes on the child's placed body, mutated by the game's own birth
 /// rule on the child's own stream, logged; without `body=`, the placed body untouched.
-- 
